  "answer": "I don't have a shell/execution tool available, so I'll verify by manual trace:\n\n**Test 1**: `mergeRanges([[8,10],[1,3],[2,5]])`\n- Validation passes; `pairs = [[8,10],[1,3],[2,5]]` (fresh copies).\n- Sort → `[[1,3],[2,5],[8,10]]`.\n- `output = [[1,3]]`.\n- `[2,5]`: `2 <= 3+1` → merge, `5 > 3` → `last[1]=5` → `[[1,5]]`.\n- `[8,10]`: `8 <= 5+1`? No → push → `[[1,5],[8,10]]`. ✓\n\n**Test 2**: `mergeRanges([[5,7],[2,4]])`\n- Sort → `[[2,4],[5,7]]`.\n- `output = [[2,4]]`.\n- `[5,7]`: `5 <= 4+1` → merge, `7 > 4` → `[[2,7]]`. ✓\n\nBoth public tests pass by trace.\n\n## Summary\n\nI rewrote `mergeRanges` in `ranges.mjs` to fix all the issues in the original implementation:\n\n| Requirement | Original bug | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| Reject malformed input with `TypeError` | No validation | Validates array, pair shape, safe-integer bounds, and `start <= end` |\n| Never mutate input | `ranges.sort()` sorted in place and mutated original pairs | Sorts a fresh `pairs` copy; each pair rebuilt as a new array |\n| Sort by start, then end | Only sorted by start | `a[0] - b[0] \\|\\| a[1] - b[1]` |\n| Merge touching/adjacent integers | `range[0] <= last[1]` missed adjacency | `range[0] <= last[1] + 1` |\n| Contained intervals must not shorten | `last[1] = range[1]` could shrink | Only extend when `range[1] > last[1]` |\n| Fresh result array | Returned references to input pairs | Builds new `output` array of fresh pairs |\n| Empty input → `[]` | Worked, but after mutation | Returns `[]` early |\n| Named export | Kept | `export function mergeRanges` |\n\nThe named export is preserved, and both public tests pass by manual trace.",
